<title>HUNGARY: CESI INDEX LOSES GROUND, ENDS AT 1,457.18 POINTS.</title>
<headline>CESI INDEX LOSES GROUND, ENDS AT 1,457.18 POINTS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index fell 0.78 percent or 11.49 points to 1,457.18 points on Tuesday, the Budapest Stock Exchange said on its Reuters page. The index, as a result of its regular review, reflects trends of 72 Hungrian, Polish, Czech, Slovak and Slovenian shares since May 2, instead of 73 shares before.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
